WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.171 --> 00:00:01.609
- [Narrator] This is Charlie Hall.

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:02.731
- Hi, I'm Charlie Hall.

00:00:02.731 --> 00:00:03.781
- [Narrator] This is
Charlie Hall's kitchen.

00:00:03.781 --> 00:00:05.789
- I make a fabulous cup of coffee.

00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:07.541
- [Narrator] This is
where Charlie Hall sleeps.

00:00:07.541 --> 00:00:09.491
- This is it, the waterbed.

00:00:09.491 --> 00:00:12.130
- [Narrator] And that bed
is whole reason we're here.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.309
- [Charlie] It's sensuous.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:16.349
It's like taking your bed to bed with you.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:20.099
- [Narrator] Charlie
Hall invented waterbeds.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:24.086
- I currently own three waterbeds.

00:00:24.992 --> 00:00:26.293
- [Narrator] Charlie
created a counterculture

00:00:26.293 --> 00:00:28.203
alternative back in the ’70s.

00:00:28.203 --> 00:00:31.381
- Remember the ‘70s and fern bars?

00:00:31.381 --> 00:00:33.203
It was like, for the groovy people.

00:00:33.203 --> 00:00:35.471
All right, you're too young for fern bars.

00:00:35.471 --> 00:00:36.813
- [Narrator] In the ’80s,

00:00:36.813 --> 00:00:38.992
they were as mainstream as they can get.

00:00:38.992 --> 00:00:40.323
- [Charlie] You could walk into any store

00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:42.643
in America and buy a waterbed.

00:00:42.643 --> 00:00:44.226
How groovy is that?

00:00:45.122 --> 00:00:46.732
- [Narrator] At their peak,
more than one in five of

00:00:46.732 --> 00:00:49.752
the beds sold in the United
States were filled with water.

00:00:49.752 --> 00:00:51.992
But it all started with
a novel idea Charlie had

00:00:51.992 --> 00:00:54.632
when he was in grad school
in the late ‘60s.

00:00:54.632 --> 00:00:57.853
He had an assignment to analyze
and improve human comfort.

00:00:57.853 --> 00:01:01.261
- [Charlie] So, I talked to
physical therapists and doctors

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:04.621
and a whirlpool bath came up
as a frequently mentioned item

00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:07.941
about a soothing temperature and water.

00:01:07.941 --> 00:01:09.323
- [Narrator] Charlie's first prototype

00:01:09.323 --> 00:01:11.093
was a chair filed with Jell-O,

00:01:11.093 --> 00:01:12.683
but there was a problem.

00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:14.053
- [Charlie] That was 300 pounds

00:01:14.053 --> 00:01:16.301
and not terribly practical
around your living room

00:01:16.301 --> 00:01:17.741
unless you had a forklift.

00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:21.203
- [Narrator] So Charlie switched
gears and focused on beds.

00:01:21.203 --> 00:01:24.941
- [Charlie] The bed evolved
into a water-filled chamber.

00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:26.512
I discovered very quickly you needed

00:01:26.512 --> 00:01:29.196
to compensate for the temperature.

00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:32.745
- [Narrator] So he added
temperature control.

00:01:32.745 --> 00:01:34.235
And when he showed the
assignment to the class.

00:01:34.235 --> 00:01:35.431
- [Charlie] Everybody loved it

00:01:35.431 --> 00:01:36.705
and they couldn't get enough of it.

00:01:36.705 --> 00:01:39.486
- [Narrator] And guess what?
Charlie got an A.

00:01:39.486 --> 00:01:42.074
- The original waterbed patent.

00:01:42.074 --> 00:01:45.777
I applied for a patent shortly
after I developed the product

00:01:45.777 --> 00:01:49.444
and I got a sense it
was gonna be a success.

00:01:53.496 --> 00:01:57.697
- [Narrator] Charlie is still
a self-proclaimed water man.

00:01:57.697 --> 00:01:59.196
This is Charlie's view.

00:01:59.196 --> 00:02:00.697
This is his boat,

00:02:00.697 --> 00:02:03.065
and this is Charlie with
his latest invention.

00:02:03.065 --> 00:02:04.055
- [Charlie] Inflatable kayaks

00:02:04.055 --> 00:02:05.305
that store in the trunk of your car

00:02:05.305 --> 00:02:08.265
and paddle like a real, nice boat.

00:02:08.265 --> 00:02:09.247
- [Narrator] Okay, that's great.

00:02:09.247 --> 00:02:10.396
Back to waterbeds.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.145
- [Charlie] The second coming is upon us.

00:02:12.145 --> 00:02:15.657
The new version will blow the
old waterbed out of the water.

00:02:15.657 --> 00:02:16.705
- [Narrator] Pun intended?

00:02:16.705 --> 00:02:18.372
- Yes, pun intended.

00:02:19.777 --> 00:02:22.444
(water rushing)

